Relevant columns & potential usage  
• "POSTAL_CODE": identify each U.S. ZIP code that reports weather observations.  
• "DATE_VALID_STD": calendar day the observations are valid for; will be filtered to 2023‑01‑15 through 2023‑01‑21.  
• "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN": total daily snowfall in inches; filter to values > 6.  
• "COUNTRY": keep only rows where value = 'US'.  

All three columns live in GLOBAL_WEATHER__CLIMATE_DATA_FOR_BI.STANDARD_TILE."HISTORY_DAY", the table that stores historical daily weather observations.

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL statements (all limited to 20 rows) that progress from simple inspection toward a final answer.  
Each statement is preceded by a brief description.

```sql
-- 1) Quick peek at snowfall data across the table
SELECT 
  "POSTAL_CODE",
  "DATE_VALID_STD",
  "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN"
FROM GLOBAL_WEATHER__CLIMATE_DATA_FOR_BI.STANDARD_TILE."HISTORY_DAY"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Distinct U.S. ZIP codes that ever recorded >6 in. of snow (no date filter yet)
SELECT DISTINCT 
  "POSTAL_CODE"
FROM GLOBAL_WEATHER__CLIMATE_DATA_FOR_BI.STANDARD_TILE."HISTORY_DAY"
WHERE "COUNTRY" = 'US'
  AND "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN" > 6
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Distinct dates in January 2023 that have any snowfall record
SELECT DISTINCT 
  "DATE_VALID_STD"
FROM GLOBAL_WEATHER__CLIMATE_DATA_FOR_BI.STANDARD_TILE."HISTORY_DAY"
WHERE "DATE_VALID_STD" BETWEEN '2023-01-01' AND '2023-01-31'
ORDER BY "DATE_VALID_STD"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Sample records for one ZIP in the week of interest
SELECT 
  "POSTAL_CODE",
  "DATE_VALID_STD",
  "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN"
FROM GLOBAL_WEATHER__CLIMATE_DATA_FOR_BI.STANDARD_TILE."HISTORY_DAY"
WHERE "POSTAL_CODE" = '01840'      -- any sample ZIP
  AND "DATE_VALID_STD" BETWEEN '2023-01-15' AND '2023-01-21'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) All days with >6 in. snowfall (no date filter) to gauge magnitude
SELECT 
  "POSTAL_CODE",
  "DATE_VALID_STD",
  "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN"
FROM GLOBAL_WEATHER__CLIMATE_DATA_FOR_BI.STANDARD_TILE."HISTORY_DAY"
WHERE "COUNTRY" = 'US'
  AND "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN" > 6
ORDER BY "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Focus on 2023‑01‑15 to 2023‑01‑21 with >6 in. snow
SELECT 
  "POSTAL_CODE",
  "DATE_VALID_STD",
  "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN"
FROM GLOBAL_WEATHER__CLIMATE_DATA_FOR_BI.STANDARD_TILE."HISTORY_DAY"
WHERE "COUNTRY" = 'US'
  AND "DATE_VALID_STD" BETWEEN '2023-01-15' AND '2023-01-21'
  AND "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN" > 6
ORDER BY "DATE_VALID_STD", "POSTAL_CODE"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) How many ZIP codes surpassed 6 in. each day of that week?
SELECT 
  "DATE_VALID_STD",
  COUNT(DISTINCT "POSTAL_CODE") AS "ZIP_CNT_GT6_IN"
FROM GLOBAL_WEATHER__CLIMATE_DATA_FOR_BI.STANDARD_TILE."HISTORY_DAY"
WHERE "COUNTRY" = 'US'
  AND "DATE_VALID_STD" BETWEEN '2023-01-15' AND '2023-01-21'
  AND "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN" > 6
GROUP BY "DATE_VALID_STD"
ORDER BY "DATE_VALID_STD"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Top ZIP codes by maximum single‑day snowfall during the target week
SELECT 
  "POSTAL_CODE",
  MAX("TOT_SNOWFALL_IN") AS "MAX_SNOW_IN_WEEK"
FROM GLOBAL_WEATHER__CLIMATE_DATA_FOR_BI.STANDARD_TILE."HISTORY_DAY"
WHERE "COUNTRY" = 'US'
  AND "DATE_VALID_STD" BETWEEN '2023-01-15' AND '2023-01-21'
GROUP BY "POSTAL_CODE"
ORDER BY "MAX_SNOW_IN_WEEK" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Compare snowfall and total precipitation on the same days (>6 in. snow only)
SELECT 
  "POSTAL_CODE",
  "DATE_VALID_STD",
  "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN",
  "TOT_PRECIPITATION_IN"
FROM GLOBAL_WEATHER__CLIMATE_DATA_FOR_BI.STANDARD_TILE."HISTORY_DAY"
WHERE "COUNTRY" = 'US'
  AND "DATE_VALID_STD" BETWEEN '2023-01-15' AND '2023-01-21'
  AND "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN" > 6
ORDER BY "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--10) Final answer query – postal code, date, snowfall >6 in. during the specified week
SELECT 
  "POSTAL_CODE",
  "DATE_VALID_STD",
  "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN" AS "SNOWFALL_IN"
FROM GLOBAL_WEATHER__CLIMATE_DATA_FOR_BI.STANDARD_TILE."HISTORY_DAY"
WHERE "COUNTRY" = 'US'
  AND "DATE_VALID_STD" BETWEEN '2023-01-15' AND '2023-01-21'
  AND "TOT_SNOWFALL_IN" > 6
ORDER BY "DATE_VALID_STD", "POSTAL_CODE"
LIMIT 20;
```
